Snapintosh is MIT with GPL-2.0 components. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists every
third-party component with its upstream notice; the licence texts are in
LICENSES/.

- compat/adreno-ib-tables.h and its generator tools/gen-adreno-ib-tables.py are
  GPL-2.0-only (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt). The CP_PROTECT table in them is
  translated from Linux drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c. A binary
  built with this table (the AdrenoX2 kext, through compat/adreno-ib-command.c,
  or a monitor build that includes it) is a combined work and is distributable
  under GPL-2.0.
- tools/qemu-sptm-oracle/qemu-sptm-oracle-tracer.patch modifies QEMU
  (jprx/qemu-sptm) and is GPL-2.0-or-later (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt),
  like the code it changes.
- Files generated from or ported from other permissively licensed projects
  (Mesa, m1n1, darwin-vm, the Linux glymur device tree) carry their upstream
  notices in addition to this licence.
- This project contains no Apple, Qualcomm, ASUS or Microsoft binaries.
  Firmware, kernelcaches, KDKs and frameworks are taken from the user's own
  machines by the provided scripts and are not covered by this licence.
